 r"I am writing to apply for the Deutsche Bank Graduate Programme in Technology, Data and Innovation in London. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have built data pipelines and AI tools that other people rely on, and turned data into decisions. I am particularly interested in this programme because its rotations combine data analysis, AI and engineering in an organisation where technology underpins the whole business.",

 r"What attracts me most to Deutsche Bank's Technology, Data and Innovation division is its focus on modernising infrastructure with cloud computing and AI, and the structured rotational programme that lets graduates build foundations across engineering, data and architecture before specialising. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and operations data in SQL and Python to identify the drivers of performance across the UK marketplace, and build KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. I also built an AI agent using Claude Code that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, and it is now used by my own team and by adjacent teams.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern for a pharmaceutical client. I built a Python pipeline that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and search augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses with an LLM-as-judge framework, and a regex and LLM extraction pipeline that turned more than 4,800 free-text consultation threads into structured data. I worked with the client's experts to design a benchmark and rubric that they adopted as their acceptance standard. Before my MSc, as a Research Data Analyst at Westlake University, I refactored and parallelised a multi-omics processing pipeline in Python and R and cut processing time by around 60 per cent, adding version-controlled scripts for reproducibility.",

 r"My MSc dissertation used 458,840 UK Biobank participants to build and validate cardiovascular risk models and estimate causal effects, delivered as an interactive Streamlit application. At Ipsos Strategy3 I built market-sizing and forecasting models and presented findings to client stakeholders, which taught me to explain technical results clearly to non-technical audiences.",

 r"I should be clear about some gaps. My degrees are in biological sciences and health data science rather than computer science, I have not yet built production systems at enterprise scale, and my cloud experience is basic. I learn new technical areas quickly and would expect the programme's training and rotations to build these foundations.",

